# Import inside the public API gateway's handle, before reverse_proxy.
# Auth password/email/metadata changes must use validated server actions and the
# internal Auth gateway. Public PUT/PATCH is limited to canonical PostgREST table
# paths. Match the request URI before any rewrite, not a decoded/cleaned path: encoded,
# repeated-slash and traversal spellings must never reach Auth through a gateway
# normalization difference. The query string does not select the upstream route.
(beanmap_public_auth_updates) {
	@disallowed_public_update {
		method PUT PATCH
		not expression `{http.request.uri}.matches('^/rest/v1/[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*([?].*)?$')`
	}
	respond @disallowed_public_update "Use the application to update account details." 405
}
